// SWARM RABBIT HOLE — Wave 15 (Impl-T, Cohort Delta): Salt ε — the
// REFUTED arm of the boundary rule. The caller passes the literal 99
// against the 3-element list literal: the engine proves the NEGATION
// (the DBM conjoins the atom, the closure hits the negative diagonal
// cycle 0 → len → 0), so the W-CONTRACT warning says the assertion
// will always fail here — and the runtime assertion still fires
// (soundness: the engine's refutation rests on the caller's facts,
// which are themselves enforced elsewhere; the fail-fast is the
// backstop). The process dies with the [E-0702] fail-fast message.

fn get(list<int> xs, int i) -> int requires(0 <= i < xs.length()) {
    return xs[i]
}

fn main() {
    list<int> xs = [10, 20, 30]
    print(get(xs, 99))
}
